Moksha is a fork of the Enlightenment 17 window manager and desktop shell,
maintained by Bodhi Linux. It is lightweight and highly configurable.

This build adds native touchpad gestures (tpgest, via libinput), the Monocle
tabbed/stacked layout, graceful close on titlebar middle click, shelves that
reserve screen space, a desk-flip spring effect, and scaling that does not
touch GTK/Qt applications.
